--[[ ==========================================================================
     ROBLOX SCRIPT DUMP  --  paste into the Studio Command Bar (View > Command Bar)

     A window opens straight away. The bar across the top tells you whether it
     can actually read your code, and if not, exactly why.

     TWO WAYS TO GET THE CODE OUT
       "Open in Script Editor"  needs nothing else. Builds the dump into real
                                ModuleScripts and opens them in Studio's own
                                editor, where Ctrl+A / Ctrl+C works properly.
       "Send to Browser"        needs  python3 dump.py  running first, plus
                                Game Settings > Security > Allow HTTP Requests.

     No -- line comments and semicolons everywhere, so this still runs even if
     the Command Bar flattens the paste onto one line.
     ========================================================================== ]]

local PORT = 8080;
